      "secrets": [
        {
          "text": "She signed the Option Clause: if the census stays under 200 for 7 days in a row, Vane Consolidated may buy the whole Wharf for a coin a metre. The loan was 40,000 coins, and the paper sits in the archive as 'Streetlight Contract.' Dunstan Frye, the archivist, keeps the key and has never opened that file.",
          "reveal": {
            "flag": "option_known"
          }
        },
        {
          "text": "A letter of resignation, dated the day before the Fellow arrived, is in her desk. Hiring the Fellow was her last try before she posted it.",
          "reveal": {
            "regard_min": 60
          }
        }
      ],
      "birthday": 8,
      "dislikes": [
        "being thanked for things she isn't proud of",
        "Vane's pocket square",
        "unanswered letters"
      ],
      "portrait": "pell",
      "pronouns": "she/her",
      "backstory": "Edwina kept the books at Pell's Hardware, so when the old mayor retired 26 years ago the council handed her the town's books too, and then the job. Arthur died six years ago; his claw hammer still hangs by her front door. Twelve years ago the mill payroll had four days of money left, and she found it. The lamps stayed lit, the wages were paid, and she has not slept a full night since. She walks the Old Quarter every dusk and counts the lamps aloud. She has told nobody how she found the money.\n",
      "workplace": "old_quarter.mayor_office",
      "appearance": "Small and upright, silver bob, half-moon glasses on a chain. Her cardigan is buttoned one hole off when she's rushed, and there is ink on her right cuff.\n",
      "occupation": "Mayor of Monde (26 years); widow of Arthur Pell of Pell's Hardware",
      "story_role": "Quest-giver and secret-keeper. D1 ferry greeting, D18 confession, D50 retirement announcement, D66 \"Pell's Choice.\" Hub of the relationship web.",
      "canon_locks": [
        {
          "fact": "Only Pell knows about the loan and the Option Clause. She deflects (lamps, the Fund, tea) and never lies outright. She does not say 'Option' or 'Vane loan.'",
          "while": "!flag.option_known"
        },
        {
          "fact": "She has confessed to the player in private and asked for a week before the town is told. She does not blame Sable for finding it.",
          "while": "flag.option_known && !flag.option_public"
        },
        {
          "fact": "She has told no one she will stand down. She announces it at the end of the Regatta on Day 50.",
          "while": "!flag.pell_retiring"
        },
        {
          "fact": "She endorses no candidate in public. She waits until Day 66 to ask the player, in private, whether they will run.",
          "while": "flag.pell_retiring && !flag.pell_asked_player"
        }
      ],
